      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Beyond My Ken",
      "description": "The Fireman's Hall Museum at 147 N. 2nd Street at the corner of Quarry Street in the Old City neighborhood of Philadelphia, Pennsylvania is located in a restored firehouse.  The building is owned by the city and the museum is run by the Philadelphia Fire Department, with the financial support of the Philadelphia Fire Department Historical Corporation.  The museum focuses on the history of firefighting in Philadelphia. (Source: Official website)",
